For the admission of DG, DG-LIST, DG-COND and DG-CASE-IF we will use
the relation O< (which is known to be well-founded on the domain recognized
by O-P) and the measure (NFIX N) for DG, (NFIX N) for DG-LIST, (NFIX N)
for DG-COND and (NFIX N) for DG-CASE-IF.  The non-trivial part of the
measure conjecture, given the :type-prescription rule REF-NAME-P, is

Goal
(AND (O-P (NFIX N))
     (IMPLIES (NOT (ZP N))
              (O< (NFIX (+ -1 N)) (NFIX N)))).
Subgoal 2
Subgoal 1
Subgoal 1'

Q.E.D.

That completes the proof of the measure theorem for DG, DG-LIST, DG-COND
and DG-CASE-IF.  Thus, we admit these functions under the principle
of definition.  We observe that the type of DG is described by the
theorem (NOT (AND (CONSP (DG X N)) (NOT (TRUE-LISTP (DG X N))))), the
type of DG-LIST is described by the theorem (TRUE-LISTP (DG-LIST XS N)),
the type of DG-COND is described by the theorem 
(NOT (AND (CONSP (DG-COND CLAUSES N))
          (NOT (TRUE-LISTP (DG-COND CLAUSES N)))))
and the type of DG-CASE-IF is described by the theorem 
(NOT (AND (CONSP (DG-CASE-IF V REST N))
          (NOT (TRUE-LISTP (DG-CASE-IF V REST N))))).

Summary
